<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29505" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏlossus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μολοσσός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Molossi,
				Molossian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">missi de gente Molossā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 226</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canes, famed for their strength,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 6, 114</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					12, 108</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gladii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 162</span></i>
			.—Also, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏlossus</span></b> ,
			i, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A Molossian</i> (hound): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Molossus acer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 405</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Molossūm for Molossorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 1063</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			prosody: pes, <i>a metrical foot consisting of three
				long syllables</i> (e. g. Arpinas, evertunt), <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				4, 82</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 475</span></i>
		P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
